# shell: desktop
# mount: /devices/board1
# board: only
# A window of the board's own, built from the desktop's kit: the same
# tabs, list, slider and field a desktop program keeps, their behaviour
# compiled for the board and their paint recorded as the desktop's own
# controls, a few hundred bytes over the console.  Each is worked from
# the desktop and the board's redraw says what changed.  This needs a
# board on the cable, so it runs only with one.
wait 30
note the board's window is on the desktop, beside its form
expect-windows 3
note the second tab is pressed and becomes current
click 558 174
wait 20
expect-title Board window
expect-narrate Switches
note a list row is chosen
click 500 248
wait 20
expect-narrate Pressure
note the slider takes the value under the pointer
click 553 325
wait 20
expect-narrate slider at 75
note the field takes the keyboard once clicked, its text selected as a
note desktop field opens, so the first letters replace it
click 500 357
wait 8
key h
key i
wait 20
expect-narrate text field "hi", focused
note and the button counts
click 421 390
wait 20
expect-narrate Pressed 1 time
shot /tmp/trk_boarddraw.png
note the window has a menu bar of its own, published as text; with the
note global bar shown, a pick on it reaches the board's process
note the window publishes a menu bar of its own, as text; with the
note global bar shown its File menu offers the board's own items
write /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings GlobalMenuBar on
wait 20
click-window Board window
wait 8
note a pick on that menu rides the wire to the board's process, which
note asks the desk for a file; the path chosen comes back over the wire
note into the field -- a menu, a process and a panel over one console
menu-pick Choose a file
wait 15
click 338 200
wait 4
click 676 413
wait 20
expect-narrate a.txt
quit
